schema: "0.4"
id: echo-of-manifestation-map-faded-chapel
type: image
quality: medium

prompt:
  text: >
    Top-down dungeon map of the Faded Chapel — Zone 1 of Echo of Manifestation, a survival horror
    roguelite. Dark fantasy game design document style, bird's-eye architectural floor plan.

    The map shows a ruined church complex with these rooms connected by shadow corridors (drawn as
    dark misty passages between rooms):

    ENTRY SHRINE (south): A small antechamber with a resonance fountain and a healing shrine. Stone
    benches line the walls. A faint amber glow emanates from the fountain. This is where the player
    begins the zone.

    COLLAPSED NAVE — COMBAT (center-south): Long rectangular hall, 24m x 10m. Crumbled pew rows form
    waist-high cover. A collapsed choir loft blocks the western flank. Three essence nodes marked as
    amber diamonds: behind altar, under loft debris, eastern pew cluster. Two shadow nodes marked as
    dark purple circles: loft rafters, confessional alcove. Falling masonry hazard zones marked with
    cracked-floor symbols.

    SEALED CONFESSIONAL — PUZZLE (west): Square room, 8m x 8m. Four confession booths with glyph-locked
    doors arranged in a 2x2 grid. One essence node at center floor mosaic. Three shadow nodes inside
    wrong-sequence booths. Whisper symbols (small sound-wave glyphs) emanate from each booth.

    RELIQUARY ANTechAMBER — LOOT (east): 12m x 10m. Dusty alcoves line the walls with deteriorated
    relics. Central stone plinth holds primary loot cache behind a faded ward. Two essence nodes:
    central plinth, northern alcove. One shadow node behind collapsed southern wall. A TIME DILATION
    POCKET marked in the northwest corner as a shimmering golden bubble behind crumbling statuary.

    UNDERCROFT PASSAGE — SECRET (subterranean, accessible from Collapsed Nave): 6m x 18m narrow
    corridor below the main floor, drawn with dashed border to indicate hidden/below. Ancient burial
    niches line both walls. Two essence nodes: end of passage, behind central burial niche. Four
    shadow nodes scattered among niches. Access trigger: baptismal font in the Nave (marked with a
    key icon).

    DESECRATED SANCTUARY — BOSS (north): Large square arena, 20m x 20m. The chapel's inner sanctum
    warped by resonance corruption. Inverted altar suspended mid-air at center. Four cracked pillars
    at cardinal positions. Four essence nodes at the pillars. Six shadow nodes: overhead rafters,
    behind altar, under floor grates. A resonance well at center marked with a danger hazard symbol.
    A TIME DILATION POCKET in the northeast corner. Boss marker: "FRACTURE WARDEN" at center with
    a skull-and-shards icon.

    THRESHOLD SHRINE (north exit): Small room beyond the boss arena with a zone gate requiring the
    resonance key from the boss. Threshold corridor leads down to Zone 2.

    Map legend in corner: Amber diamond = Essence Node, Purple circle = Shadow Node, Golden bubble
    = Time Dilation Pocket, Dashed border = Secret Room, Skull icon = Boss, Arrow = Shadow Corridor.

    Style: Architectural blueprint quality, drawn on aged parchment-toned background. Room walls in
    dark charcoal lines with dusty gold and faded crimson tinting. Shadows and atmospheric haze around
    corridor connections. Professional game design document aesthetic. Clean labels in serif font.
    Slight vignette around edges.
  negative: "bright colors, cartoon style, anime, 3D rendered, photorealistic, messy hand-drawn, childlike, bright lighting, cheerful, low detail"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1536
    aspect_ratio: "1:1"

tags: [map, zone-1, faded-chapel, top-down, dungeon-map, game-design-document, dark-fantasy]
